:{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/png"}],"revisions":[{"revid":1222789091,"parentid":992840493,"timestamp":"2026-05-30T09:39:04Z","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"=={{int:filedesc}}==\n{{Information\n| description    = {{en|1=Shoulder Sleeve Insignia (SSI) of the Eastern Defense Command, part of the United States Army.}}\n| date           = 1943-11-27\n| source         = [https://tioh.army.mil/Catalog/Heraldry.aspx?HeraldryId=15962&CategoryId=9234&grp=2&menu=Uniformed%20Services&from=search Eastern Defense Command SSI] from the United States Institute of Heraldry website\n| author         = {{Creator:United States Army}}\n| permission     = \n| other versions = \n}}\n\n== Description ==\n'''Blazon'''\n\n''On a shield 2 3/4 inches (6.99 cm) in height and 2 inches (5.08 cm) in width divided horizontally red and blue by a 1/16 inch (.16 cm) yellow partition line invected two yellow tridents in saltire, all within a 1/8 inch (.32 cm) yellow border''.\n\n'''Symbolism'''\n\nThe colors red, blue and yellow are representative of the three arms composing the Eastern Defense Command:  Artillery, Infantry and Cavalry, while the tridents and the invected partition line which suggests waves are representative of the Coastal Defense functions of the organization.\n\n'''Background'''\n\nThe shoulder sleeve insignia was approved on 27 November 1943.\n\n=={{int:license-header}}==\n\n{{PD-USGov-Military-Army-USAIOH}}\n\n[[Category:1943 works in the United States]]\n[[Category:Shoulder Sleeve Insignia of the United States Army (SSI)]]"}}}]}]}}